  "id": "DrugBank_DB01003 - MONDO_4979",
  "verbalization": "Cromoglicic Acid is associated with Asthma through a series of indirect pathways, primarily via the indication of Intrinsic Asthma and Allergic Asthma. These pathways link Cromoglicic Acid to Ibudilast, which in turn is indicated to treat Asthma. The evidence suggests that Cromoglicic Acid may exert a therapeutic effect on Asthma by influencing the biological processes underlying the condition, possibly through the modulation of inflammatory responses or bronchoconstriction. The presence of multiple pathways, including those involving Ibudilast, indicates a potential role in the treatment of Asthma, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of Asthma pathophysiology and the potential for Cromoglicic Acid to interact with multiple components of the disease.",
